---
import Component from "../../../src/components/donate/MomentumTestimonials.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for the impact band as the campaign design draws it: alternating
// photo/quote rows on aqua, under a kicker, a serif heading, and a slotted lede.
//
// The two quotes are deliberately UNEQUAL. The first carries a portrait and the
// second does not, which is the production state — there is no photo on file for
// Mohammed Ally, and the card is built to render without one rather than borrow
// a face that is not his. A frame where both had portraits would hide the case
// that actually ships.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: MomentumTestimonials-PhotoRows</title>
    <style is:global>
      /* The rows are two columns only at a page-like width; the fit-content
         wrapper would stack every photo above its quote. */
      #codeyam-capture {
        width: 1200px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="codeyam-capture">
      <Component
        kicker="Every number represents a story"
        title="One connection can change what's possible."
        testimonials={[
          {
            quote:
              'I moved to the Bay Area knowing almost no one in tech. The first Harvard Alumni in Tech event I walked into, I met three people who are still in my corner two years later. That is not networking. That is a community deciding you belong.',
            name: 'Jessica Li',
            affiliation: 'Harvard University Alumni · Class of 2019',
            role: 'San Francisco Event Lead',
            photo: '/images/team/jessica-li.png',
            eventPhoto: '/images/gallery/event-07.jpg',
            eventCaption: 'Leaders in Engineering · San Francisco',
            order: 1,
          },
          {
            quote:
              'Colorado did not have a chapter. We started with six people in a co-working space on a Saturday afternoon. What the fund pays for is the part nobody sees — the space, the coffee, the follow-up that turns a one-time afternoon into something people plan their month around.',
            name: 'Mohammed Ally',
            affiliation: 'Harvard Extension School Alumni · Class of 2023',
            role: 'HIT Colorado Co-Event Lead',
            eventPhoto: '/images/gallery/event-11.jpg',
            eventCaption: 'HIT Colorado Co-working Afternoon · Improper City',
            order: 2,
          },
        ]}
      >
        <p>
          Behind every event, chapter, and member of our network is a conversation, an introduction,
          or a shared experience that helped someone move forward. These are a few of them, in the
          words of the people they happened to.
        </p>
      </Component>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
